  "reviewer_notes": "This is a scenario-based LCA+DEA technology assessment, not a fitted statistical energy performance model. The three 'models' (EPI, UEPI, TPI) are CCR-DEA efficiency formulations differing only in which input/output indicators enter (Table 2). DEA has no dependent variable in the regression sense, no goodness-of-fit or out-of-sample validation, and no fixed coefficients (weights are computed endogenously per DMU); these are coded not applicable / not reported accordingly. C3 'role' does not map cleanly to DEA — all inputs and outputs were coded 'predictor' since they jointly determine the efficiency score; excluded variables (alumina, aluminum products, NOx) recorded on M1. Data are LCA figures per 1 ton aluminum, calculated primarily from GREET software (coded data_type simulation). Scale coded 'facility' by inference; the actual scope is a whole aluminum production supply chain (power generation + electrolysis + processing) for which no exact scale enum exists. Sector 'steel and primary metals' is inferred (aluminum is a primary/nonferrous metal).",
